@Here’s Johnny 

Typically you have a computer program which helps you fill around your theme (or seed entries) and gives you options. It may give you options you never heard of and you may look them up to see who or what they are, or see how often they’ve been used in other puzzles (if they’ve been used a few times, especially in the NYT, you will have more confidence that they are fair and legit). Personally I try to avoid names or words that I haven’t heard of, to make sure the puzzle has my personality and is fair by my standards; but sometimes it’s unavoidable and you have to compromise. That said DIONNE Warwick and
LEEZA Gibbons are well within my wheelhouse and famous by my standards, and I’d have no trouble using them as long as I thought the crosses were fair and the overall use of proper nouns was reasonable.
